Z||000011||TRiAD||06-10-2001||10:06 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>I've seen that car in person at the Carlisle show a few weeks ago. It is absolutely awesome. The fit and finish is better than any factory built car. It's really amazing. But it doesn't look like an authentic Lamborghini, and it should not be advertised as one. I'm not sure how much of it is Fiero, if any. I don't think it's worth anything close to $175,000. But it is nice.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, it says it's got Rayne suspension, and a V8 Archie V8 (or as he put it, "Archi") kit, so I suppose it's mostly Fiero. <BR>And yes, since it was brought up...real Diablos are coming in under $100K now. In fact, if you don't mind a few miles (over 2000), I could get you <B>2</B> for his starting bid!<P>...I'm glad I'm not alone in thinking "bigboystoys" is out of line on this one...<BR>Thanks!<P><BR>BTW, can anyone tell if this is really an LT1?<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://abacus.sj.ipixmedia.com/abc/M28/4fe233fbe7005736c6324ec1a5/i-2.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 06-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Predator||06-10-2001||10:28 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> $175,000.00 my god this guy must be high on something.. Unless this thing sprouts wings and flys it might be worth what he wants for the deposit. I need to go into the kit car business. Man I had no idea the V8 Archie kit increased the value of a car so much  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I can't stop laughing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">..<BR>Wouldn't it be funny if somebody actually placed a bid on it.. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
