Z||000017||ElricSI||06-10-2001||11:45 PM||||I think you guys are forgetting about the free trailer.  But it looks like the nicest kit Fiero I have ever seen.  I would say it might be worth around 50,000.<P>But what do I know.<P>------------------<BR>Proud Owner of 85 GT||||reg||6
Z||000018||Tweek||06-11-2001||12:14 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B><P>I wonder if that 84 SE really used to be an Indy or if it's just a very good forgery.<P>But I'm NOT cynical.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well... It was the wrong interior, and the wrong decklid. BUT, all on any true indy if you put it through a vin checker it will say SE. Putting that vin true the checker at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.net</A>  you get this:<P>1 Made in USA  <BR>G Made by GM  <BR>2 Pontiac Division  <BR>A Fiero (P-Body)  <BR>F SE  <BR>37 NotchbackNotchback  <BR>R 2.5L L4 (LR8)  <BR>8 Check Digit  <BR>E 1984  <BR>P Made in Pontiac, MI  <BR>268564 68564 of 136,840  <P>Reading back through the auction again, the seller acccounts for these changes...  (though if I had a nice indy it would stay stock) Im betting my $64 thats its a true Indy<p>[This message has been edited by Tweek (edited 06-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||BAM-BAM||06-11-2001||12:19 AM||||b  Well, I E-Mailed him and asked a couple of questions; is it a corvette LT1 and is it a true Diablo or a kit rebody? Here is what he had to say: <P>yes to the engine. not a diablo or kit. in between.<P> So now you know it's not a real Diablo and it is an LT1. I don't quite get what is meant by "in between". It's a Fiero base, that's obvious, just look at the engine hatch, it has Rodneys supports on it and then the mention of an ARCHI engione kit. Perhaps Archie would know who it is? Anyway, way to much $$$ even with the trailer. heck for $70,000.00 more you could get a brand new Shelby Series 1.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||1
Z||000020||fyerstarter||06-11-2001||01:15 AM||||You forgot to ask him is he was INSANE!!!!  :P||||reg||1
Z||000021||AusFiero||06-11-2001||03:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87GT:<BR><B>Did anybody see the 69 Trans-Am Convertible with a manual tranny on ebay?  It was one of only 8 Trans-Am convertibles that year and somebody was auctioning it for $175,000 with the reserve not yet met.  It was a beautiful car but $175,000?!??!?!  I dont know about that.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would like to see him prove it is one of the 8 original 69 TA Convertibles. There is an awful lot of copies around of them. I seen a website that had pictures of 10 of the "original" 8 produced. Work that 1 out.<P>He is having a real wank at that price anyway. One of the original 69 TA convertibles resides in Australia and has GM papers to say it is a real one with all the right bits on it. From memory all the convertibles were auto anyway (don't quote me on that but I am pretty sure thats what the Firebird red book says).<P>The one here in Australia is LHD, restored to showroom condition and can be had for US$35,000. Certainly a lot less than US$175,000.<P>Gotta love E-Bay. Anyone wanna buy a 1957 Coke Bottle. I will let if go for only $25,000  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000022||Formula||06-11-2001||09:38 AM||||I saw that car at carlisle too....<P>not worth 175k imo, maybe worth 50k but I would buy an authentic sports cr fo that price, ex. used viper, corvette etc...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
