Z||000024||Yellow88GT||06-11-2001||11:23 AM||||That picture is not of an LT1 !<P>I had one in my 95 Formula Firebird and that<BR>is not it. The intake runner on an LT1 does<BR>NOT have the 8 tube drops, the L98 does.<P>IMHO that is an L98 (the motor chevy had before the LT1)<P>Still a 350 but no reverse flow cooling,<BR>way lower HP, etc.<P>Jerry||||reg||13
Z||000025||Toddster||06-11-2001||11:46 AM||||Pontiac Enthusiast Magazine did an article on Pontiac Pace Cars last year. They valued a Fiero Indy with under 20,000 miles at $10,000. (There were 2001 made according to the article)<P>The Indy above has the Y82 option code according to the owner so it is a real Indy. And at less than half that price, I'd say its a good value considering it would only cost $1000 or so to completely restore it.<P>Of all the Ebay Fieros up right now, I gotta say this is the best value....Of course I'm still giving that $175,000 dollar Lambo a good long think.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000026||TRiAD||06-11-2001||02:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fyerstarter:<BR><B>Intrepid Tail Lights, 300ZX Headlights, ....how "exotic"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually the 300ZX headlights are used on all current Diablos. One of the few things he did "right". <P>||||reg||1
Z||000027||drednot||06-11-2001||02:46 PM||||I just had to e-mail this quy!  <P>"This is FRAUD!!!  You never disclose that this is simply a very well done Kit car.  Man, Just looking at it, it has PONTIAC FIERO written all over it, hmmmm you never mention that.  I do like those Dodge Intrepid T-lights, kind of funny.  Hey, you know you could buy about 25 REAL Dodge Intrepids for that price!  Just to let you know, you are NOT going to get and real bids on the thing.  It's just too funny!!  You are being laughed at all over the internet in probably about 4000 different message boards!!  If You are trying to sell this thing right, list it under PONTIAC FIERO!!!"<P>||||reg||10
