Z||000041||Voytek||06-12-2001||02:22 PM||||Ok.  I'll tell you what these things go for.  Rehberg Motorsports in Vancouver, Canada is selling turnkeys for $40,000 to about $80,000 USD.  The top models are roadsters and include all options (air, cruise, PM,PDL,PW, etc.), removable top, all leather interior, all vented disc brakes upgrade, an LT1 engine and Porsche 911 tranny.  The cars are Fiero based but look like the real thing.  Some of you suggested $50,000 USD.  That's too low, but $175,000 ??!!!!  BTW, check out the window curve.  Looks kinda familiar, doesn't it?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000042||Toddster||06-12-2001||07:05 PM||||$75k makes sense. It's still high but at least it has the right number of digits.<P>My guess is that $60k is the right price, assuming it was well built and comes with a warranty. ||||reg||1
Z||000043||Jay in Atlanta||06-12-2001||10:03 PM||||The thing looks remarkably like a Lear:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.lear2000.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lear2000.com</A> <P>I would have thought it was Lear that did it, if it hadn't been for the pretentious "Archi" (heh, heh) namedropping.  If Lear did do the build with the Chevy 350, it would be $68K plus customization.<P>~Jay<BR>black '85 2m4 5-speed<p>[This message has been edited by Jay in Atlanta (edited 06-12-2001).]||||reg||1
